cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Spatiotemporal Responses of AIS-Broadcasting Fishing Vessels to
  Offshore Wind Development in Southern New England
message: If you use this software or its outputs, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: McCaffrey
    given-names: Malachy
    affiliation: University of Rhode Island
repository-code: https://github.com/Malachy-McCaffrey/gfw_fishing_osw_ais
abstract: >-
  Open-source geospatial workflow quantifying AIS vessel presence and apparent
  fishing effort across three phases of offshore wind development at the
  Orsted South Fork, Revolution and Sunrise Wind projects in Southern New
  England. Implements Global Moran's I, Getis-Ord Gi* hotspot analysis, Anselin
  Local Moran's I cluster and outlier analysis, and stage-to-stage hotspot
  transition analysis using geopandas, libpysal and esda.
keywords:
  - offshore wind
  - fisheries
  - AIS
  - spatial statistics
  - Global Fishing Watch
  - hotspot analysis
# license: add once a LICENSE file is chosen (see README)
date-released: '2026-09-02'
references:
  - type: database
    title: Global Fishing Watch AIS-based vessel presence and apparent fishing effort
    year: 2026
    notes: >-
      Accessed via the 4Wings API using gfwr v3.0. Data licensed CC BY-SA 4.0.
    url: https://globalfishingwatch.org
